# {{projectName}}

This is your independent pnpm monorepo. Application source and defaults are yours
to edit; the source template repository is not needed to run this project.

## Start here

```sh
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm bootstrap --source default
pnpm apps:list
pnpm dev --app <app-name>
pnpm build --all
pnpm validate
```

A bare workspace has no app to start. Its shared packages still build and validate.
To add an app, run this from the template source repository:

```sh
pnpm template:clone --target <this-project-directory> --name web
pnpm template:clone --target <this-project-directory> --name editor --template studio
```

The app name is required. The default app template is plain-next. These operations
preserve existing apps/packages and create one separate commit per added app.

## Own the project

- Edit pages in apps/<name>/src/app and starter declarations in src/site.
- Edit tracked resource defaults or use the app's ignored .local overrides; then
  prepare explicitly with pnpm app:prepare --app <name>.
- Starter mechanisms live in src/infra. You may replace them when needed.
- packages/shared contains neutral capabilities. packages/site and
  packages/adapters contain optional domain and service/runtime implementations.
- Each app README explains its examples and which example routes can be removed.

